§ `Income Tax Ordinance — credit points — the persons the sections speak of`

-- s 1, line 108: ”אדם“ – לרבות חברה וחבר בני־אדם, כהגדרתם בסעיף זה;
-- s 1, line 124: ”חבר בני אדם“ – כל גוף ציבורי, מואגד או מאוחד, וכל חברה ...
-- ss 34 and 36 speak of a "יחיד" (an individual), a word s 1 does not define;
-- s 36A speaks of an "אשה" (a woman), also undefined. The Ordinance's own
-- contrast is between an individual and a body of persons, so a person is one
-- or the other, and only an individual carries the facts below.
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `an individual`     HAS `the individual` IS AN Individual
    `a body of persons`

DECLARE Individual HAS
    -- s 1, lines 143-162, "תושב ישראל" (a): an individual whose centre of life
    -- is in Israel, with the rebuttable day-count presumptions of para (2).
    -- The test is NOT encoded (NOTES.md coverage table): this field carries the
    -- status as determined under s 1 for the tax year in question, and nothing
    -- else. ss 34 and 36 both read it; see fork F3 on their different wording.
    -- (0.2.0) s 3A(f), line 471, treats an Israeli citizen who is a resident
    -- of the Area, or who operates in the Area, "as if" an Israeli resident.
    -- That is NOT entered here: it is carried by the two s 3A(f) facts of
    -- `Taxpayer in a tax year` below, which the rules over that record read.
    -- The year-free rules over a Person do not take those facts, so they
    -- cannot see s 3A(f) (NOTES.md, version 0.2.0).
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                   IS A BOOLEAN

    -- s 36A, line 1597: בחישוב המס של אשה
    -- "אשה" is not defined in the Ordinance (fork F9). (0.3.0) Under Meng's
    -- ruling SHRUG of 2026-10-08, F9 is an input convention, not a switch:
    -- the caller determines who is a woman, and no rule reads it two ways.
    `a woman`                                               IS A BOOLEAN

    -- s 48, line 1807: גם לגבי תושבי אזור שאינם אזרחים ישראליים
    -- Residents of the Area (as s 3A, lines 455-461, defines "אזור" and
    -- "תושב אזור") who are not Israeli citizens. Read only to route such a
    -- person to the refusal for s 48, which is not encoded.
    -- (0.2.0) "Israeli citizen" has the meaning s 3A(a) gives it, which s 48
    -- adopts ("כהגדרתם בסעיף 3א"), and that meaning is wider than citizenship:
    -- line 457: (2) תושב ישראל;
    -- line 458: (3) מי שזכאי לעלות לישראל לפי חוק השבות, התש״י–1950, והוא תושב אזור;
    -- So an individual who is an Israeli resident in the tax year is an
    -- "Israeli citizen" here, and this field cannot truthfully be TRUE for
    -- such an individual.
    `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen`  IS A BOOLEAN

    -- s 48A, line 1811: ”עובד זר“ – כהגדרתו בחוק עובדים זרים ... אף אם רואים אותו כתושב לענין פקודה זו
    -- A foreign worker as the Foreign Workers Law 5751-1991 defines one, even if
    -- treated as a resident. Read only to route such a person to the refusal
    -- for s 48A and its 2014 Regulations, which are not encoded.
    `a foreign worker`                                      IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Income Tax Ordinance — credit points — a taxpayer in a tax year (0.2.0)`

-- The record the year-aware rules read (ito-s34-s36-s36a-credits.l4). It adds
-- to a Person the two things the year-free rules never asked: which tax year
-- is being computed, and the facts of s 3A(f). It is a separate record, not
-- new fields of `Individual`, so that every existing construction of an
-- `Individual` (the independent tests', the capstone's) stands unchanged.
-- (0.3.0) It also carries the two facts forks F2 and F4 ask: income from
-- personal exertion, and residence for only part of the tax year.
DECLARE `Taxpayer in a tax year` HAS
    `the taxpayer`                                          IS A Person

    -- line 202: ”שנת מס“ – תקופה של שנים עשר חדשים רצופים, שתחילתה ב־1 בינואר
    -- Written as the calendar year in which the tax year begins, e.g. 2025.
    -- A special assessment period (the definition's second limb) is not
    -- distinguished.
    `the tax year`                                          IS A NUMBER

    -- line 471: (ו) בכפוף להוראות סעיף זה, יחולו על אזרח ישראלי שהוא תושב אזור או פועל באזור, הוראות פקודה זו כאילו היה תושב ישראל
    -- s 3A(f) has two limbs, one fact each. "Israeli citizen" is s 3A(a)'s
    -- (lines 455-459): a citizen under the Citizenship Law 5712-1952, an
    -- Israeli resident, a person entitled to immigrate under the Law of Return
    -- 5710-1950 who is a resident of the Area, or a body of persons such a
    -- person controls. "Resident of the Area" is s 3A(a)'s "תושב אזור"
    -- (line 461): the s 1 residence test with "the Area" for "Israel".
    -- Limb (i): an Israeli citizen who is a resident of the Area.
    `an Israeli citizen who is a resident of the Area`      IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Limb (ii): an Israeli citizen who operates in the Area ("פועל באזור",
    -- which the Ordinance does not define; an input, like "אשה", fork F9).
    `an Israeli citizen who operates in the Area`           IS A BOOLEAN

    -- (0.3.0) Fork F2. s 1 defines "הכנסה מיגיעה אישית" inclusively:
    -- line 170: ”הכנסה מיגיעה אישית“ – לרבות –
    -- Whether the taxpayer had such income in the tax year, as the caller
    -- determines it; read only under the readings of s 36 that ask it.
    `the taxpayer had income from personal exertion in the tax year` IS A BOOLEAN

    -- (0.3.0) Fork F4. Whether the residence status entered on the
    -- individual held for the whole tax year, or the individual was an
    -- Israeli resident for only some of its months (arriving or leaving
    -- during the year). Read only under the readings of ss 34 and 36 that
    -- ask it.
    `the taxpayer's Israeli residence over the tax year`    IS AN `Israeli residence over the tax year`

-- (0.3.0) Fork F4: the residence entered on the individual held for the whole
-- tax year, or for only some months of it.
DECLARE `Israeli residence over the tax year` IS ONE OF
    `the residence entered held for the whole tax year`
    `an Israeli resident for only part of the tax year` HAS
        -- a whole number from 1 to 11
        `the months of the tax year in which the taxpayer was an Israeli resident` IS A NUMBER

§ `Income Tax Ordinance — credit points — the readings of forks F1, F2 and F4 (0.3.0)`

-- RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): where the text does not decide, one
-- named switch per fork, by default a refusal by name where the readings give
-- different answers, every reading kept by name. NOTES.md, fork register.

-- Fork F1: does s 36A (line 1597) require the woman to be an Israeli
-- resident, as ss 34 and 36 beside it say of theirs?
DECLARE `A reading of section 36A on residence` IS ONE OF
    `section 36A has no residence condition`
    `section 36A gives its half point only to an Israeli resident`
    `declined where residence decides section 36A`

-- Fork F2: does s 36's quarter point "as a travel credit" (line 1594),
-- under the heading of a credit for travel to the place of earning (line
-- 1593), need income from personal exertion?
DECLARE `A reading of section 36 on income from personal exertion` IS ONE OF
    `section 36 for every resident individual`
    `section 36 only for an individual with income from personal exertion`
    `declined where income from personal exertion decides section 36`

-- Fork F4: what do ss 34 and 36 give an individual who was an Israeli
-- resident for only part of the tax year?
DECLARE `A reading of sections 34 and 36 for part of a tax year` IS ONE OF
    `one residence status for the whole tax year`
    `apportioned by the months of residence, as section 41 apportions`
    `declined for residence in part of a tax year`

DECLARE `The readings of forks F1, F2 and F4` HAS
    `fork F1, section 36A and residence`                     IS A `A reading of section 36A on residence`
    `fork F2, section 36 and income from personal exertion`  IS A `A reading of section 36 on income from personal exertion`
    `fork F4, residence for part of a tax year`              IS A `A reading of sections 34 and 36 for part of a tax year`
